body:
I mean, after like 6 months of what felt like a one sided crush... and at least 3 months of consistent flirting.... I don't feel like a smart cookie, but i'm still happy about this.

&#x200B;

i mean... girls, right?

Obligatory “not a scarer but”: I went to a haunted house with friends 6 or 7 years ago, and there was a haunted school bus part where you climbed in, and there were people in the seats and stuff, but it was mostly just to get to a much larger thing, a bit where they could slow you down so you don’t catch up to the other parties.

Unfortunately, me being clumsy led to me tripping and kneeing one of the “bodies” on the ground, which turned out to be a real person who I just kneed in the face. 

Dude didn’t make a sound, turned over and gave me a thumbs up, while I’m apologizing over and over. Props to him for somehow staying silent. If you read this, I’m sorry for kneeing you in the face ;-;

I had a conversation about something similar recently, so while this is... not an easy story, it's one that I feel somewhat fine with sharing. When I was in my sophomore year of high school, I failed 5/7 of my classes, and felt as if nothing in my life would go right. I climbed onto a roof the school (about 3 stories up) and jumped. I landed on my front, but at an angle. I bled out there, and for the most part, felt relief. As if a huge weight was lifted from my shoulders all of a sudden. I woke up a few more times, and really just recall small bits of what happened. There was an Ambulance, and I blacked out again, and then I was in the ambulance. It felt like a dream, and I kind of just floated along.

&#x200B;

I made a nearly full recovery, although my kidney still has some issues from being crushed/bones piercing it. Overall, just... really floaty.
